# Per-unit network hostname, read by TeamViewer Host as the default device name.
#
# Provisioning writes the customer name once, and it persists across reboots:
#     setprop persist.sys.tepari_device_name "<customer name>"
#
# The '=*' trigger fires when the property is written at runtime, and again on
# every boot: init replays persistent properties through the normal property
# path once /data is mounted, which re-runs property triggers. init only fires
# a '=*' trigger for a non-empty value, so an unprovisioned unit simply leaves
# net.hostname unset, exactly as it is today.
#
# This must be installed to system_ext (or system/product), never to vendor or
# odm. setprop from a vendor/odm init script runs in the vendor_init SELinux
# domain, which is not granted set_prop for system_prop -- the context of both
# net.hostname and persist.sys.* . system_ext runs in the init domain.

on property:persist.sys.tepari_device_name=*
    setprop net.hostname ${persist.sys.tepari_device_name}
